2
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:44,200
みなさん、こんばんは！ハロー！
Everyone, good evening! Hello!

3
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:49,000
こんばんは！ハロー！
Good evening! Hello!

4
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
ということで、まずは自己紹介からやっていきましょう。
With that, let's start with introductions.

5
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:58,200
ホロライブの清楚担当、みんなのアイドルの夏色まつりです！
I'm Natsuiro Matsuri, Hololive's seiso representative and everyone's idol!

6
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:02,000
今日はMCを務めさせていただきます。頑張ります！
I'll be the MC today. I'll do my best!

7
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,400
じゃあ、今日参加してくださる皆さんの自己紹介を
Now, let's have the participants introduce themselves

8
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:08,800
1人ずついきますよ。
one by one.

9
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:11,200
じゃあ、よぴぴからお願いします！
Let's start with Yopipi!

10
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:14,600
はい！イオフォリア・オフィサロ、どうもです。
Yes! Ioforia Ofisaro, hello.

11
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:17,600
ホロライブインドネシアから、イオフィです！
I am Iofie from Hololive Indonesia!

12
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:22,000
今日は、オノマトペをちょっと…
Today, I'd like to study a bit

13
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,300
勉強したいと思います。よろしくお願いします！
about onomatopoeia. Please look after me!

14
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:27,700
お願いします！じゃあ、コボちゃん。
Thank you! Next, Kobo-chan.

15
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:34,400
わこわこ！わこかなえる！At your service, let me be your sun, shine your day.
Waku waku! Kobo Kanaeru at your service, let me be your sun, shine your day.

16
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,400
こぼ・かなえる、れんしゃ…めーそ
Kobo Kanaeru... [struggling with Japanese]

17
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:40,400
今日のは、オノマトペは…
Today, for onomatopoeia...

18
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:44,800
勝ちだ！お願いします！
I'm gonna win! Please look after me!

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,400
じゃあ、続いてジジ！
Next up, Gigi!

20
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:55,300
こんばんは、ジジです。アイム・オニ！
Good evening, I'm Gigi. I'm an Oni!

21
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,000
えーっと、日本語ちょっと上手くない。
Uh, my Japanese isn't very good.

22
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,000
オノマトペ、うーん、ちょっと…
But I'll do my best with onomatopoeia

23
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,500
日本語頑張って、頑張ります！
and Japanese! I'll do my best!

24
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:13,400
ありがとう！頑張れ！
Thank you! Do your best!

25
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:16,800
はい、続いて、ほぼJPのべーちゃん。
Yes, next is Bae-chan, who is basically JP.

26
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:20,500
いやいやいや、ワサワサ！我々はカオス、ハコス・ベールズです。
No, no, no! Waza waza! We are Chaos, Hakos Baelz.

27
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:24,800
今日は翻訳担当でやりたいと思います。よろしくお願いします！
Today, I'll be acting as the translator. Please look after me!

28
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:29,800
よろしくお願いします！
Please look after us!

29
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:32,400
じゃあ、最後は、ラオラ。
Alright, and lastly, Raora.

30
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:35,800
あっ、こんにちは。ラオラ・パンテーラです。
Ah, hello. I am Raora Panthera.

31
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:40,000
今日は、えーっと、絵を描いたり、
Today, I'll do my best drawing

32
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:45,300
日本語で話したり、頑張ります！
and speaking in Japanese!

33
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:51,300
チャオ！よろしくお願いします！
Ciao! Please look after me!

34
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:55,000
はい、おねがいします。ということで、本日はですね、
Yes, thank you. So today,

35
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,200
みなさんにオノマトペクイズに答えてもらいます。
we'll have everyone answer an onomatopoeia quiz.

36
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:02,800
ちょっとね、日本独特の表現とかもたくさんあるんですが、
There are many uniquely Japanese expressions,

37
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:06,000
頑張って答えてね。
but please do your best to answer!

38
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:12,000
日本に来るときは、いっぱい使っていただきたいなと思います。
When you come to Japan, I'd love for you to use them a lot!

39
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,600
はい、ということで！
Alright, with that!

40
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:17,600
早速、第1問、いきましょう。
Let's go straight to the first question!

41
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:22,000
クエスチョン1！
Question one!

42
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:27,500
このオノマトペは、何を表しているでしょうか。
What does this onomatopoeia represent?

43
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:31,500
「コケコッコー」
"Kokekokkoo"

44
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:36,500
コケコッコー？何これ？
Kokekokkoo? What is this?

45
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,500
Where do you hear this onomatopoeia from?

46
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
わからない！
I don't know!

47
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
あ、じゃあ、ヒントは、
Ah, then here's a hint.

48
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,500
動物の鳴き声ですね。
It's an animal's cry.

49
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,800
なんの動物の鳴き声でしょう。
What animal's cry is it?

50
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:00,000
It's an animal cry! What animal makes this sound?

51
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:01,808
あれ？
Huh?

52
00:05:01,808 --> 00:05:03,108
ちょっと待って、ペンが…
Wait a minute, my pen...

53
00:05:03,108 --> 00:05:06,108
ペンがおかしいんです、私。なんで？
My pen is acting weird. Why?

54
00:05:06,108 --> 00:05:09,108
あ、書けない？
Oh, you can't write?

55
00:05:09,108 --> 00:05:11,808
コケコッコー
Cock-a-doodle-doo.

56
00:05:11,808 --> 00:05:14,008
ケコケコッコッコ
Cack-cack-cackle-cackle.

57
00:05:14,008 --> 00:05:16,808
ペンがおかしい。あれ？なんでこうなっちゃうんだろう？
My pen is weird. Why is it doing this?

58
00:05:16,808 --> 00:05:19,408
ケコケコッコッコ
Cack-cack-cackle-cackle.

59
00:05:19,408 --> 00:05:21,408
書けるかな？
Can I draw?

60
00:05:21,408 --> 00:05:25,508
ちょっと待ってください、アプリ再起動します。すみません。
Please wait a moment, I'll restart the app. Sorry.

61
00:05:25,508 --> 00:05:28,008
Should we draw?

62
00:05:28,008 --> 00:05:30,508
You can do whatever, you can just write it.

63
00:05:30,508 --> 00:05:35,008
I drew it because I don't know what it is in Japanese!

64
00:05:35,008 --> 00:05:36,208
It's alright.

65
00:05:36,208 --> 00:05:38,208
I don't know the word.

66
00:05:38,208 --> 00:05:40,508
何々？あれ？
What is it? Huh?

67
00:05:40,508 --> 00:05:43,008
書けるかな？
Can you write it?

68
00:05:43,008 --> 00:05:45,008
あ、書けます！
Ah, I can write!

69
00:05:45,008 --> 00:05:46,508
あ、よかった。
Oh, good.

70
00:05:46,508 --> 00:05:48,008
よかった。
Good.

71
00:05:48,008 --> 00:05:50,008
終わった。
Finished.

72
00:05:50,008 --> 00:05:51,508
コケコッコー
Cock-a-doodle-doo.

73
00:05:51,508 --> 00:05:54,008
声に出したらわかるかも。
If you say it out loud, you might understand.

74
00:05:54,008 --> 00:05:56,508
コケコッコー
Cock-a-doodle-doo.

75
00:05:56,508 --> 00:05:58,208
鳥？
Bird?

76
00:05:58,208 --> 00:06:00,008
大丈夫かい？
Are you okay?

77
00:06:00,008 --> 00:06:03,508
コケコッコー、コケコッコーでしたよ。
It was cock-a-doodle-doo.

78
00:06:03,508 --> 00:06:05,508
コケコ！
Cackle!

79
00:06:05,508 --> 00:06:10,508
おー。OK、じゃあ、一人ずつ聞いていきましょう。じゃあ、よぴぴ、何だと思いますか？
Oh. Okay, then, let's ask one by one. So, Yopipi, what do you think it is?

80
00:06:10,508 --> 00:06:13,008
あ、チキンです！
Ah, chicken!

81
00:06:13,008 --> 00:06:15,508
お、チキン！はいはいはい。
Oh, chicken! I see, I see.

82
00:06:15,508 --> 00:06:18,008
にわとりね、はい。
A rooster, right.

83
00:06:18,008 --> 00:06:21,008
はい、じゃあ、コボちゃん。
Yes, next, Kobo-chan.

84
00:06:21,008 --> 00:06:26,008
Ah, before I was thinking about frog, but I think "koke-kokko" is...

85
00:06:26,008 --> 00:06:29,508
It sounds like Indonesian "kukuruyuk"!

86
00:06:29,508 --> 00:06:33,008
So, it's chicken!

87
00:06:33,008 --> 00:06:36,508
おお！なるほど！
Oh! I see!

88
00:06:36,508 --> 00:06:38,208
なるほどね。
I see.

89
00:06:38,208 --> 00:06:44,508
なんか、元々カエルだと思ってたんだけど、なんかインドネシアのオノマトペでも…
She thought it was a frog at first, but in the Indonesian onomatopoeia...

90
00:06:44,508 --> 00:06:52,008
オノマトペに、なんかニワトリの音に似てるので、チキン。なるほど。
...it sounds like a rooster, so chicken. I see.

91
00:06:52,008 --> 00:06:59,008
はい、じゃあ、ジジ。
Yes, next, Gigi.

92
00:06:59,008 --> 00:07:08,008
えー、ケコケコッコッコ、英語は... Cock-a-doodle-doo! Chicken.
Well, cackle cackle cackle, in English it's... Cock-a-doodle-doo! Chicken.

93
00:07:08,008 --> 00:07:11,008
同じだね、チキン。じゃあ、べっちゃん。
The same, chicken. Then, Bae-chan.

94
00:07:11,008 --> 00:07:16,508
あ、僕もニワトリ、チキン。だと思います。
Ah, me too, rooster, chicken. I think so.

95
00:07:16,508 --> 00:07:19,508
はい、じゃあ最後はラオラ。
Yes, and finally, Raora.

96
00:07:19,508 --> 00:07:24,008
Ah... for me it's like a bird that is screaming like "koko",

97
00:07:24,008 --> 00:07:28,008
...like "I'm here!" and...

98
00:07:28,008 --> 00:07:30,508
あ、ココ？
Oh, "here"?

99
00:07:30,508 --> 00:07:38,008
He wants food in his mouth because maybe he is small, you know, I don't know.

100
00:07:38,008 --> 00:07:40,008
Bae-chan, what do you think it is? A bird?

101
00:07:40,008 --> 00:07:44,008
Bird? Sakebutori.

102
00:07:44,008 --> 00:07:46,008
鳥、叫ぶ鳥ね。
A bird, a screaming bird, right.

103
00:07:46,008 --> 00:07:50,008
お腹空いている叫ぶ鳥ね。
A hungry screaming bird, right.

104
00:07:50,008 --> 00:07:54,008
了解。
Roger.

105
00:07:54,008 --> 00:07:58,008
じゃあ、正解いきましょう。正解は...
Then, let's see the correct answer. The correct answer is...

106
00:07:58,008 --> 00:08:01,008
チキン！ニワトリでした！
Chicken! It was a rooster!

107
00:08:01,008 --> 00:08:05,508
You got it! Yay!

108
00:08:05,508 --> 00:08:10,008
まあ、正解にしますか。叫ぶ鳥だもね。
Well, should we count it as correct? It is a screaming bird.

109
00:08:10,008 --> 00:08:13,508
叫ぶ鳥は鳥。鳥は鳥、同じだからね。素晴らしい。
A screaming bird is a bird. A bird is a bird, it's the same. Wonderful.

110
00:08:13,508 --> 00:08:21,008
Everybody gets a point! Yay!

111
00:08:21,008 --> 00:08:31,008
コケコッコー、コケコッコーでした。
Cock-a-doodle-doo, it was cock-a-doodle-doo.

112
00:08:31,008 --> 00:08:34,008
はい、じゃあ続いて、第２問。
Yes, now for the second question.

113
00:08:34,008 --> 00:08:37,008
こちらも動物の鳴き声でございます。
This is also an animal sound.

114
00:08:37,008 --> 00:08:41,008
Oh, the second question is also the sound of an animal.

115
00:08:41,008 --> 00:08:45,008
はい、第２問はこちら。ケロケロ。
Yes, the second question is this: Kero-kero (ribbit ribbit).

116
00:08:45,008 --> 00:08:48,008
あ、ケロケロ！
Oh, kero-kero!

117
00:08:48,008 --> 00:08:51,008
Easy! Easy!

118
00:08:51,008 --> 00:08:55,008
ケロケロ。
Ribbit ribbit.

119
00:08:55,008 --> 00:09:00,008
書けるかな？
Can you draw it?

120
00:09:00,008 --> 00:09:03,008
べっちゃん、それは… え？
Bae-chan, that is... What?

121
00:09:03,008 --> 00:09:08,508
ええ？すごい！
Huh? Amazing!

122
00:09:08,508 --> 00:09:12,008
何？何？何？何？
What? What? What? What?

123
00:09:12,008 --> 00:09:16,008
Eh, my pen... Okay, it works.

124
00:09:16,008 --> 00:09:21,008
ケロケロ、ケロケロ、ケロケロ…
Ribbit ribbit, ribbit ribbit...

125
00:09:21,008 --> 00:09:24,008
ケロケロ。かわいい、ケロケロ。
Ribbit ribbit. Cute, ribbit ribbit.

126
00:09:24,008 --> 00:09:28,008
ラオラ、大丈夫？
Raora, are you okay?

127
00:09:28,008 --> 00:09:32,008
Oh, yes, okay. Okay, it's working. Thank you.

128
00:09:32,008 --> 00:09:35,008
べっちゃんの何？
What is Bae-chan's?

129
00:09:35,008 --> 00:09:40,008
え？
What?

130
00:09:40,008 --> 00:09:43,008
Wait, hold on, I forgot what it looks like!

131
00:09:43,008 --> 00:09:45,008
Is that an owl?

132
00:09:45,008 --> 00:09:47,008
What are you drawing?

133
00:09:47,008 --> 00:09:50,008
Why is she drawing herself?

134
00:09:50,008 --> 00:09:53,008
I forgot what it looks like!

135
00:09:53,008 --> 00:09:56,508
べっちゃんの…
Bae-chan's...

136
00:09:56,508 --> 00:10:00,008
It looks like a chimera, you know. Chimera-like.

137
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:01,216
きめるわ
I'm locking it in!

138
00:10:01,216 --> 00:10:03,016
Oh my god! きめるのやめて
Oh my god! Don't lock it in!

139
00:10:04,016 --> 00:10:09,016
おっしゃ、ちょっと1人ずつまた聞いていきますか？
かわいいみんな。
Alright, let's ask everyone one by one.
You all drew so cutely.

140
00:10:09,016 --> 00:10:11,016
えー、じゃあ、よっぴぴ！
Let's start with Yoppipi!

141
00:10:11,016 --> 00:10:13,516
あい！カエル、Frogです。
Yes! It's "kaeru", a frog.

142
00:10:13,516 --> 00:10:17,516
あ、Frog。ケロケロ。でしょ？
Oh, frog. Ribbit-ribbit. Right?

143
00:10:17,516 --> 00:10:19,516
うんうん、なるほど。あい！
Right, right. I see. Yes!

144
00:10:19,516 --> 00:10:22,516
じゃあ続いて、コボちゃん！
Next up is Kobo-chan!

145
00:10:22,516 --> 00:10:27,516
私もカエル！カエル、はい。
ケロケロ、ケロケロ。
Me too, a frog! A frog, yes.
Ribbit-ribbit, ribbit-ribbit.

146
00:10:27,516 --> 00:10:30,516
ケロケロ。
Ribbit-ribbit.

147
00:10:30,516 --> 00:10:34,016
すごーい！
Awesome!

148
00:10:34,016 --> 00:10:37,016
まつりも書けないの？カエル。
Matsuri, can't you write "kaeru" either?

149
00:10:37,016 --> 00:10:39,516
はい、続いて、ジジ！
Alright, next up, Gigi!

150
00:10:39,516 --> 00:10:41,516
はい！ケロケロ、ケロッピー！
Yes! Ribbit-ribbit, Keroppi!

151
00:10:41,516 --> 00:10:45,016
あ、ケロケロケロッピー？おー！
Ah, Kero Kero Keroppi? Oh!

152
00:10:45,016 --> 00:10:47,016
なるほど。じゃあ、べーちゃん！
I see. Next, Bae-chan!

153
00:10:47,016 --> 00:10:49,016
あ、カエルです。
Ah, it's a frog.

154
00:10:49,016 --> 00:10:51,016
お？カエルかな？
Oh? Is it a frog?

155
00:10:51,016 --> 00:10:52,516
カエルです。
It's a frog.

156
00:10:52,516 --> 00:10:56,516
カエーーール！カエーーール！
Frog! Frog!

157
00:10:56,516 --> 00:10:59,516
一瞬ネズミに見えたんだけど。
For a second, it looked like a mouse to me.

158
00:10:59,516 --> 00:11:03,516
確かにね、カエル見たことないんで。
True, since I've never seen a frog.

159
00:11:03,516 --> 00:11:08,516
一応カエル。カエル。カエルが白枠。
But it's supposed to be a frog.
A frog. In the white frame.

160
00:11:08,516 --> 00:11:12,516
その隣の、ラオラ、めっちゃ絵うまい。かわいい！
Next to her, Raora,
you're so good at drawing. Cute!

161
00:11:12,516 --> 00:11:15,016
かわいい！
So cute!

162
00:11:15,016 --> 00:11:17,016
カエルですね？
It's a frog, right?

163
00:11:17,016 --> 00:11:20,016
うん。カエルです。
Yeah, it's a frog.

164
00:11:20,016 --> 00:11:23,016
はい。じゃあケロケロ、正解は？
Alright, so "kero kero"...
the correct answer is...

