Eh? Are there none?

691
00:45:26,572 --> 00:45:31,072
いや、いるとは思うんだけど、声は聞こえるけど、姿がなんかどこにいるのかわかんない。
No, I think they're around, and I can hear them, but I don't know where they are, like their physical appearance.

692
00:45:31,072 --> 00:45:35,072
そうんだ。え、子供の頃セミ捕りとかしないの？
Oh, I see. Did you not catch cicadas when you were kids?

693
00:45:35,072 --> 00:45:36,572
ない。
No.

694
00:45:36,572 --> 00:45:40,572
あれは多分、結構なんか日本文化的な...
That's probably a very Japanese cultural thing...

695
00:45:40,572 --> 00:45:42,572
ああ、へー！そうなんだ！
Ah, I see!

696
00:45:42,572 --> 00:45:44,272
ないない。
No, we don't.

697
00:45:44,272 --> 00:45:47,572
じゃあ、セミの種類とか言われてもあんまわかんないのか。
So if we talk about cicada species, you don't really know them?

698
00:45:47,572 --> 00:45:50,072
わかんない！全部セミだもん！
We don't! They're all just cicadas!

699
00:45:50,072 --> 00:45:52,072
確かに。
True.

700
00:45:52,072 --> 00:45:55,072
そうなんだ。
Is that so?

701
00:45:55,072 --> 00:45:59,072
Anyone of you guys caught cicadas before? Caught us...
Have any of you guys caught cicadas before?

702
00:45:59,072 --> 00:46:03,072
Cicada? Ever caught one before?

703
00:46:03,072 --> 00:46:05,072
No.

704
00:46:05,072 --> 00:46:08,572
I got one in my balcony.
I got one on my balcony.

705
00:46:08,572 --> 00:46:09,572
え？
Eh?

706
00:46:09,572 --> 00:46:10,572
Your balcony?
On your balcony?

707
00:46:10,572 --> 00:46:11,572
Yeah.

708
00:46:11,572 --> 00:46:12,572
Balcony?!

709
00:46:12,572 --> 00:46:14,572
It was huge! It was like super big!

710
00:46:14,572 --> 00:46:16,872
And it was super loud!

711
00:46:16,872 --> 00:46:18,072
バルコニーに？
On the balcony?

712
00:46:18,072 --> 00:46:19,372
ベランダ、ベランダね。
Veranda, veranda.

713
00:46:19,372 --> 00:46:21,072
ベランダにいた？
It was on the veranda?

714
00:46:21,072 --> 00:46:22,072
そんなに大きいの？
Was it that big?

715
00:46:22,072 --> 00:46:23,072
セミって。
A cicada?

716
00:46:23,072 --> 00:46:25,572
結構デカいよ。よくいるよ、その辺で死んでるのとか。
They're pretty big. You often see dead ones lying around.

717
00:46:25,572 --> 00:46:28,072
マジ？！
Seriously?!

718
00:46:28,072 --> 00:46:30,072
Big bug.

719
00:46:30,072 --> 00:46:32,072
コボは大丈夫とかな？
I wonder if Kobo is okay with them?

720
00:46:32,072 --> 00:46:34,072
大丈夫くない。
I'm not okay.

721
00:46:34,072 --> 00:46:36,072
大丈夫くない！何回も聞いていいよ。
She's not okay! You can listen to it again.

722
00:46:36,072 --> 00:46:38,072
大丈夫じゃない？
You're not okay?

723
00:46:38,072 --> 00:46:40,072
何回も。大丈夫ない。
Again. I'm not okay.

724
00:46:40,072 --> 00:46:43,072
Can I have a hint?

725
00:46:43,072 --> 00:46:46,072
ヒント！ヒントお願い！
Hint! Hint please!

726
00:46:46,072 --> 00:46:50,072
ヒントは、なんかあの「ショワショワショワ」って言ってるのは無視していい。
The hint is, you can ignore the "showa showa showa" sound.

727
00:46:50,072 --> 00:46:57,072
その、大きい低めの音のセミさんはなんて言ってるかだね。
Listen to what the loud, lower-pitched cicada is saying.

728
00:46:57,072 --> 00:46:59,072
おお。
Oh.

729
00:46:59,072 --> 00:47:04,072
Focus on the lower sounding notes, ignore the "showa showa" in the background.

730
00:47:04,072 --> 00:47:07,072
困ってるね。
We're in trouble.

731
00:47:07,072 --> 00:47:11,072
オッケー。
Okay.

732
00:47:11,072 --> 00:47:15,072
オッケー、じゃあ行きましょう。よぴぴから。
Okay, let's go. Starting with Yopipi.

733
00:47:15,072 --> 00:47:18,072
はい。みー、みー...
Yes. "Mee, mee..."

734
00:47:18,072 --> 00:47:22,072
はいはい、みーみーみーみー、はい。
Yes, yes. "Mee, mee, mee, mee," yes.

735
00:47:22,072 --> 00:47:23,072
みーね、オッケー。
"Mee," okay.

736
00:47:23,072 --> 00:47:24,072
じゃあ、コボちゃん。
Then, Kobo-chan.

737
00:47:24,072 --> 00:47:26,072
ちー...
Chee...

738
00:47:26,072 --> 00:47:27,072
ちー...
Chee...

739
00:47:27,072 --> 00:47:28,072
かわいい。
Cute.

740
00:47:28,072 --> 00:47:30,072
ちー、ちー。
"Chee, chee."

741
00:47:30,072 --> 00:47:35,072
ちーだね、かわいい。
It's "chee." Cute.

742
00:47:35,072 --> 00:47:36,072
はい、じゃあジジ。
Okay, next is Jiji.

743
00:47:36,072 --> 00:47:40,072
ジジは、じーじーじーじーじー...
Jiji is "jee-jee-jee-jee-jee..."

744
00:47:40,072 --> 00:47:46,072
ジジの鳴き声！
Jiji's call!

745
00:47:46,072 --> 00:47:47,072
おお。
Oh.

746
00:47:47,072 --> 00:47:49,072
じゃあ、続いてべちゃ。
Then, next is Becha.

747
00:47:49,072 --> 00:47:51,072
え、
Uh...

748
00:47:51,072 --> 00:47:54,072
うぃーー！
Wryyyy!

749
00:47:54,072 --> 00:47:57,072
うぃー、オッケーオッケー。
"Wryy," okay, okay.

750
00:47:57,072 --> 00:47:59,072
じゃあ、ラスト、ラナ。
Then, last is Rana.

751
00:47:59,072 --> 00:48:02,072
あ、えーと、くり、くり、くり、くり...
Ah, um, "kuri, kuri, kuri, kuri..."

752
00:48:02,072 --> 00:48:05,072
あ、かわいい、「くりくり」。
Ah, cute, "kuri-kuri."

753
00:48:05,072 --> 00:48:08,072
オッケーオッケー。
Okay, okay.

754
00:48:08,072 --> 00:48:10,072
じゃあ、正解いきましょう。正解は、
Now, let's see the correct answer. The correct answer is...

755
00:48:10,072 --> 00:48:14,072
はい。
Yes.

756
00:48:14,072 --> 00:48:18,072
みーーんみんみんみんで、よぴぴ正解！
"Mee-ee-n min min min," Yopipi is correct!

757
00:48:18,072 --> 00:48:19,072
やった！
Yay!

758
00:48:19,072 --> 00:48:22,072
It doesn't sound like "min min" at all.

759
00:48:22,072 --> 00:48:28,072
聞こえないんだよね、M。Mの音なくない？
You can't hear the "M," right? Isn't there no "M" sound?

760
00:48:28,072 --> 00:48:29,072
There is no M sound.

761
00:48:29,072 --> 00:48:33,072
このセミの名前がそもそも「ミンミンゼミ」という名前のセミね。
The name of this cicada is originally "Minmin-zemi."

762
00:48:33,072 --> 00:48:37,072
あ、ミンミンゼミ。
Ah, Minmin-zemi.

763
00:48:37,072 --> 00:48:43,072
「みーんみんみんみん」って日本人には聞こえてます。
It sounds like "mee-n min min min" to Japanese people.

764
00:48:43,072 --> 00:48:44,072
へー。
I see.

765
00:48:44,072 --> 00:48:47,072
じゃあ、続いてネクストセミいきますよ。
Now, moving on to the next cicada.

766
00:48:47,072 --> 00:48:49,072
ネクストセミ？
Next cicada?

767
00:48:49,072 --> 00:48:52,072
One more セミいきます。
Let's do one more cicada.

768
00:48:52,072 --> 00:48:55,072
One more セミ？
One more cicada?

769
00:48:55,072 --> 00:49:01,072
セミ2、こちらです。じゃあ、皆さんにも聞かせます。
Cicada 2 is this one. Let's let everyone hear it.

770
00:49:01,072 --> 00:49:05,072
はい。セミ2。
Yes. Cicada 2.

771
00:49:05,072 --> 00:49:07,072
What is this?

772
00:49:07,072 --> 00:49:11,072
なにこれ？！
What is this?!

773
00:49:11,072 --> 00:49:15,072
What is this sound from?

774
00:49:15,072 --> 00:49:19,072
I don't know.

775
00:49:19,072 --> 00:49:22,072
What the heck?!

776
00:49:22,072 --> 00:49:25,072
Haha, what the...

777
00:49:25,072 --> 00:49:39,072
セミバージョン2ですよ。
This is cicada version 2.

778
00:49:39,072 --> 00:49:47,072
What is this?

779
00:49:47,072 --> 00:49:51,072
わかるかな？セミ2ね。
Do you know it? Cicada 2.

780
00:49:51,072 --> 00:49:55,072
ヒントお願いします！
Hint, please!

781
00:49:55,072 --> 00:49:57,072
ヒント！
Hint!

782
00:49:57,072 --> 00:50:00,072
ヒントは...
The hint is...

783
00:50:00,080 --> 00:50:01,380
ヒントは...
What is...

784
00:50:01,380 --> 00:50:03,280
ヒントは？
What's the hint?

785
00:50:03,280 --> 00:50:08,080
あの、タタタタターン、タタタタターンっていうのが、鳴き声。
Well, the call goes "ta-ta-ta-ta-taan, ta-ta-ta-ta-taan".

786
00:50:08,080 --> 00:50:09,180
タタタタターン？
Ta-ta-ta-ta-taan?

787
00:50:09,180 --> 00:50:10,580
タタタタターン。
Ta-ta-ta-ta-taan.

788
00:50:10,580 --> 00:50:17,380
が、日本人には、タ・タ・タ・タ・タン、だからまあ、5文字くらいかな？
To Japanese people, it's "ta-ta-ta-ta-tan", so maybe about 5 characters?

789
00:50:18,080 --> 00:50:20,080
え？5？
Huh? Five?

790
00:50:20,080 --> 00:50:23,080
Can you focus on the sound that makes that pattern?

791
00:50:23,080 --> 00:50:25,080
うーん、パターン？
Hmm, pattern?

792
00:50:25,080 --> 00:50:27,580
ヒント難しいね、これは。
Giving hints is hard for this one.

793
00:50:27,580 --> 00:50:29,380
ヒントとして難しいな。
As a hint, it's hard.

794
00:50:29,380 --> 00:50:36,480
その、タタタタターンもオノマトペだと言われたら、もうごめんなさい、それは...
If you say "ta-ta-ta-ta-taan" is also onomatopoeia, then I'm sorry, that is...

795
00:50:36,480 --> 00:50:37,780
えー？ むず...
Huh? Hard...

796
00:50:37,780 --> 00:50:44,280
もうダダダダダしか聞こえへん。
I can only hear "da-da-da-da-da".

797
00:50:44,280 --> 00:50:46,380
うーん、意味...
Hmm, the meaning...

798
00:50:46,380 --> 00:50:50,080
You got this, guys. We got this.

799
00:50:50,080 --> 00:50:54,480
まあ、伸ばし棒が入ります、あと、最後の方に。
Well, there is a macron (elongated vowel) at the end.

800
00:50:54,480 --> 00:50:55,280
え？
Eh?

801
00:50:55,280 --> 00:51:00,080
There is an elongated... there is an elongated sound?

802
00:51:00,080 --> 00:51:01,380
伸ばすと7文字ですね。
If you include the elongated sound, it's 7 characters.

803
00:51:01,380 --> 00:51:02,380
ええ？
Eee?

804
00:51:04,080 --> 00:51:06,080
ちょっと、諦め用に流しとくか。
Maybe I should play it again to help you give up.

805
00:51:06,080 --> 00:51:08,580
難しいね。
It's difficult.

806
00:51:08,580 --> 00:51:10,580
This is, this voice...

807
00:51:10,580 --> 00:51:15,080
リズム、実体は分かるんだけど、どう書いていいか分からない。
I can understand the rhythm itself, but I don't know how to write it.

808
00:51:15,080 --> 00:51:16,480
落ち着く。
Calming.

809
00:51:16,480 --> 00:51:20,080
ね。
Yeah.

810
00:51:20,080 --> 00:51:23,780
この、この声を聞くと落ち着きますよ。夏だなって。
If you hear this voice, you feel calm. Like, "Ah, it's summer."

811
00:51:23,780 --> 00:51:25,080
ええ？
Eee?

812
00:51:25,080 --> 00:51:27,580
How is this sound relaxing to Japanese people?

813
00:51:27,580 --> 00:51:29,080
ええ？
What?

814
00:51:29,080 --> 00:51:31,280
ええ？落ち着くよね？
Huh? It's calming, right?

815
00:51:31,280 --> 00:51:33,080
Okay.

816
00:51:36,080 --> 00:51:39,080
じゃあ、いきましょうか。よぴぴから。
Then, let's go. Starting with Yopipi.

817
00:51:39,080 --> 00:51:43,380
いや、ク・ク・ク・ク・クじゃないですか？セミ バージョン２。
No, isn't it ku-ku-ku-ku-ku? Cicada version 2.

818
00:51:43,380 --> 00:51:44,780
セミ バージョン２？
Cicada version 2?

819
00:51:44,780 --> 00:51:50,080
セミ、ク・ク・ク・ク、オッケー？
Cicada, ku-ku-ku-ku, okay?

820
00:51:50,080 --> 00:51:51,580
オッケー、オッケー。じゃあ、じーちゃん。
Okay, okay. Then, Gigi-chan.

821
00:51:54,080 --> 00:51:58,280
Um... so...

822
00:51:58,280 --> 00:52:02,380
The previous one was min-min, right?

823
00:52:02,380 --> 00:52:03,780
うん。アハ。
Yeah. Aha.

824
00:52:03,780 --> 00:52:12,380
And, uh, I heard this is more than min-min, so it's a mating call like 'mang mang, mang mang!'

825
00:52:13,280 --> 00:52:15,580
ちょっと待って。
Wait a minute.

826
00:52:15,580 --> 00:52:18,080
そもそも, why did you write 'mating call'?
First of all, why did you write "mating call"?

827
00:52:18,080 --> 00:52:21,080
えーと、求愛の鳴き声。ミンミンです。
Uh, mating call. It's min-min.

828
00:52:21,080 --> 00:52:24,080
あ、でも求愛の鳴き声なんだよね、実際。
Ah, but actually, it is a mating call.

829
00:52:24,080 --> 00:52:25,580
あ、そうなの？
Oh, really?

830
00:52:25,580 --> 00:52:27,080
そう、そう。Yes.
Yes, yes. Yes.

831
00:52:27,080 --> 00:52:30,080
Wait, so it is a mating call! It's a mating call!

832
00:52:30,080 --> 00:52:33,280
Oh my god!

833
00:52:33,280 --> 00:52:39,080
セミのオスが、あの、メス来て！って言ってる時の声だから、そこは正しい。
It's the sound of a male cicada saying "Hey, females, come here!", so that part is correct.

834
00:52:39,080 --> 00:52:44,280
ええー！ Oh my god, oh my god!
Eee! Oh my god, oh my god!

835
00:52:44,280 --> 00:52:45,380
It is?

836
00:52:45,380 --> 00:52:48,080
でも、でも、ミンミンが正しいかどうかね。
But, but, whether "min-min" is correct or not...

837
00:52:48,080 --> 00:52:50,080
あっ、そう、ミンミンね、オッケー。
Ah, right, min-min, okay.

838
00:52:50,080 --> 00:52:51,580
Whether it's min-min or not.

839
00:52:51,580 --> 00:52:54,080
オッケー、ということで。チチ。
Okay, so. CC.

840
00:52:54,080 --> 00:52:59,780
Um, tsuku-tsuku-g, tsuku-tsuku-g, tsuku-tsuku-g...

841
00:53:00,080 --> 00:53:03,080
オッケー、ツクツクGオッケーね。
Okay, tsuku-tsuku-G is okay.

842
00:53:03,080 --> 00:53:05,580
じゃあ、べちゃん。
Then, Be-chan.

843
00:53:05,580 --> 00:53:10,080
え？なんか... puku-puku-puku-puka! Puku-puku-puku-puka!
Eh? Like... puku-puku-puku-puka! Puku-puku-puku-puka!

844
00:53:10,080 --> 00:53:13,280
ポケモンっぽかったんだけど。
That sounded like a Pokemon.

845
00:53:13,280 --> 00:53:16,480
ポケモン... puku-puku, puku, puku-puku-puka.
Pokemon... puku-puku, puku, puku-puku-puka.

846
00:53:16,480 --> 00:53:18,080
オッケー。
Okay.

847
00:53:18,080 --> 00:53:20,080
じゃあ、ラオーラ。
Then, Raora.

848
00:53:20,080 --> 00:53:28,080
In my opinion, it's a cricket, and the cricket sounds like 'pring pring, pring pring!'

849
00:53:28,080 --> 00:53:30,080
ぷりんぷりん、可愛い。
Pring pring, cute.

850
00:53:30,080 --> 00:53:32,480
Pring pring, pring pring.

851
00:53:32,480 --> 00:53:34,080
But it's a cricket!

852
00:53:34,080 --> 00:53:36,080
For you.

853
00:53:37,080 --> 00:53:40,080
じゃあ、いきます。こちらの鳴き声は...
Okay, here we go. This call is...

854
00:53:40,080 --> 00:53:43,780
ツクツクボウシでございます！
Tsukutsukuboushi!

855
00:53:43,780 --> 00:53:46,580
えええー！
Eeee!

856
00:53:46,580 --> 00:53:50,080
何、何で？何で？何で？Why?
What, why? Why? Why? Why?

857
00:53:50,080 --> 00:53:57,080
ツクツクボウシ、ツクツクボウシ、ツクツクボウシ、ツクツクボウシ！
Tsukutsukuboushi, tsukutsukuboushi, tsukutsukuboushi, tsukutsukuboushi!

858
00:53:57,080 --> 00:54:00,080
So I should do this if I want to mating call someone?

859
00:54:00,080 --> 00:54:05,080
ツクツクボウシ！ Not tsuku-tsuku-G?
Tsukutsukuboushi! Not tsuku-tsuku-G?

860
00:54:05,080 --> 00:54:13,280
Not tsuku-tsuku-G, 求愛の鳴き声。
Not tsuku-tsuku-G, it's a mating call.

861
00:54:13,280 --> 00:54:19,080
Tsukutsukuboushi! Sha-please! Sha-please!
Tsukutsukuboushi! Shut up, please! Shut up, please!

862
00:54:21,580 --> 00:54:26,580
まあ、ツクツクボウシか、ツクツクホウシ、どっちでもオッケー。
Well, tsukutsukuboushi or tsukutsukuhoushi, either is okay.

863
00:54:26,580 --> 00:54:29,080
ツクツクホウシ？どっちでもオッケーです。
Tsukutsukuhoushi? Either is okay.

864
00:54:29,080 --> 00:54:33,080
ツクツクホウシ、ツクツクホウシ... となっております。はい。
Tsukutsukuhoushi, tsukutsukuhoushi... That's what it is. Yes.

865
00:54:33,080 --> 00:54:36,580
ちょっとね、これセミは難しいですね。
Yeah, cicadas are difficult.

866
00:54:36,580 --> 00:54:40,080
セミの種類とかは関係ないんですか？
Does the species of cicada not matter?

867
00:54:40,080 --> 00:54:44,580
あ、これはツクツクボウシっていうセミの鳴き声ですね、今のは。
Ah, this is the call of the cicada species called "Tsukutsukuboushi", the one just now.

868
00:54:44,580 --> 00:54:49,080
あ、種類？そう、種類もツクツクボウシっていう名前のセミ。
Ah, species? Yes, the species itself is also a cicada named "Tsukutsukuboushi".

869
00:54:49,080 --> 00:55:00,080
ちなみに他にも、さっきのがミンミンゼミだったでしょ？アブラゼミっていうのが、あの、ジジがさっき言ってた、ジジジジジジジって泣くのがアブラ...
By the way, the previous one was Minminzemi, right? Aburazemi is the one that goes "ji-ji-ji-ji-ji-ji" like Gigi was saying...

870
00:55:00,088 --> 00:55:01,088
セミだったり
...like a cicada...

871
00:55:01,088 --> 00:55:02,188
アブラゼミ
Aburazemi.

872
00:55:02,188 --> 00:55:03,288
はい。
Yes.

